A||N||16||FieroSTETZ||different forms of forced induction?||||1||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||07-27-2000||02:23 AM||||a few questions on forced induction (was gonna get a new engine but cant get any response from fieroshop...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ) i know the pluses/minuses of turbocharging and such, as well as supercharging... would it be possible to use both? like a tiny supercharger for more bottom end and a huge turbo that kicks in later? i know that it'd probably be only okay for racing, but? thoughts on superchargers that might work... would the supercharger out of a thunderbird SC work on one of our cars? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FIEROCIOUS||07-27-2000||02:36 AM||||A turbo charger will give you good torque down low you just have to size the turbine correctly for your application. Turbos have recieved a bad rap. Differant sizes need differant spool time. <P>Twin turbos use two turbos ran sequentualy to flaten the powerband. The smaller turbo boosts at low RPM's and the larger for high RPM's. <P>To reduce turbo lag it is best to run the (largest) exhaust pipe posible.A turbo is  like a pinwheel (if you put your hand directly behind it it won't spin.)<P>The T3's that are being used on Fieros are a good compromise for a street daily driver if power is more your likeing you can use a T3/T4 hybrid with good results.<P>One other note if you race the Fiero it won't drop below 3500 rpm so low rpm torque doesn't matter.<P>If autocross is your goal a turbo may not be the best.<P>Has anyone autocrossed a turbo Fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000002||olympic||07-27-2000||02:55 AM||||  I saw a cool set up an a wild Chevy Typhoon.  It was turbo charged(of course) but they added a 40hp shot of nitrous to cover up the turbo lag.  The N2O would only engage at full throttle and only for a couple seconds.  They claimed over 400 hp at the wheels and it could smoke all 4 tires at once.  Awesome.   But Fierocious is right.  A well built turbo system will have minimal lag.  Newer cars like the Audi TT have no noticeable lag at all.  Older cars like the turbo T-birds gave turbos a bad rap.<P>   As for the SC off of a T-bird I dont think it will work.  You would need a custom intake to mount the blower unit to your heads.  The blower doesn't just bolt on to any intake.<P>   Heres a question I've always wondered about.  Since the Syclone/Typhoon used left over Gran National parts did GM use the same all wheel drive set up in them as the Astro/Safari vans have???  If this was true it probably wouldn't be hard to install the Astro van tranny and front axle into an S10 and make your own home made Syclone.  Could even add a V8 to make it simpler.<P>------------------<BR>Your best...???  Losers whine about doing their best.   Winners go home and f*** the prom queen! - Sean Connery in "The Rock"||||reg||3
Z||000003||86SE||07-27-2000||03:05 AM||||i wish that air compressor thing worked.....<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||1
