Z||000005||loafer87gt||07-27-2000||12:56 PM||||RS's website is webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/ <P>They are the guys building up my 3.0 190 HP v6 for me. They are super guys to deal with over the phone, and I've ordered stuff from them before and never had any problems.||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||07-27-2000||01:18 PM||||HKS of Japan makes a kit for the AE86 Corolla, and 1st gen MR2 to "Twin Charge" it. uses a TD-04 and the toyota SC14 (1.4 liter superchager from 94 previa) So do CMN Custom Network Motors (fuel tuners on my SE)they make a kit to Twin charge a Starion/Conquest. it is a good idea but the engine management and getting all the wastegates to work at the right time so you're never out of boost either way.. or over pressureizing and roasting head gaskets.. Paeco( in Birmingham,Al.) makes dead soft copper head gaskets for these high pressure applications. $82 each. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||BBBAD GT||07-27-2000||01:58 PM||||Keep in mind the different types of blowers on the market.  A centrifugal and positive displacement type blowers are completely different in the way it forces the air in.  <P>It really depends on what you want.<P>BTW, I saw a 502 cu in crate motor in a 454SS truck with a whipple blower (positive dispacement) on it last weekend.  How much low end torque do you need? Sheeeesh.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif"> <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||07-27-2000||03:22 PM||||I never owned a supercharged car. but my 86 has a small airesearch turbo. Not a rocket out of the hole, but it really pulls hard over around 40mph and pulls and pulls. Its a rush seeing how fast itll kick over 100. I dont notice any lag at all for the turbo coming on boost and for daily driving i run with 4-5 lbs boost, and it sounds awsome too.<P>rg<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||GT Bastard||07-28-2000||10:15 PM||||Roger, is your turbo setup custom built by yourself?  If so, are you using the MSD-BTM?||||reg||1
Z||000010||HYPTNOTiSE||07-30-2000||12:51 PM||||Come on now! Is everyone forgetting nitrous?!? Nitrous is possibly the best bang for the buck out there. It does start to feel expensive if you use it alot, because you have to get the jug filled, fairly often if you use it a lot. But still i'd have to use a lot of nitrous to even come close to the price of a supercharger or turbo. But for me and street driving mostly, I'd go with a supercharger. I like turbo setup's i love them, but personally i dont like hours, days, and months of tuning, just to get it so you can drive it, then more tuning till it's perfect. You see turbo guys run at the track, one pass they'll run 11.0 and the next a 15.5. Untill you get them tuned they're so unreliable. I just dont want a car, spitting and sputtering, and popping and cracking, and through soot out the exhuast when i have 3-4G's invested in a turbo system. But they're always the tried and true miller-woods turbo kit. No tuning required, that's all been taken care of. Personally i'm going to buy racetech's vortec supercharger kit when it comes out. But if you wanna slap a power adder on in one day and go very fast, very cheap. Get nitrous.<P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Sillhouette.com||07-30-2000||04:37 PM||||Hey Carefull with Race Tech!<P>They have not built a supercharger kit yet but advertize that they have.  Their problem is the computer part of the system.  Anyone can hook up a supercharger but not a lot of people can deal with the change in engine management.  <BR>RSM has already built and sold a few kits throught North America.  They have been runnign a car with this kit on it for over a year and no problems.  <BR>Your choice of what you want to do but just be carefull with Race Tech I have witnessed a lot of bad stuff from there.  <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000012||HYPTNOTiSE||07-30-2000||10:29 PM||||Personally i'm not going to be using a fiero computer, i'm going to use an Accel DFI programable unit, so i dont think i have to worry about they're chip much. I did talk to them about a couple weeks ago, and they did mention that they're chip was finished. But the thing is with racetech they actually use a quality supercharger. You all will soon see the reliability that the rotrex holds. Not much. I've dealt with them and know people that use them, and they have they're fair share of problems. And since EIP tuning, stopped selling them, there are no US dealers any longer, so parts are going to take a while to get here from Europe, and i'd imagine they're going to be pricy. I have also talked with many technitions at EIP and they refer to the rotrex supercharger as a peice of junk, that has to be rebuilt every 20,000miles.  They were unhappy with them and thats why they no longer sell them. Vortec's are made and sold by many retailers across the US. They're a tried and true charger. I believe that racetech's kit is going to come with a quality adjustable blow off valve. Not a plastic one set to blowoff at 15psi. I don't know how well racetech's kit is designed as of yet. I haven't seen any pics, But I don't think it will take much to top RSM's kit. When it's finally released, i may buy it if it's a quality product, but if not i'll  design my own system. I'd only have minor changes to make to my buddy's accel program, so tuning isn't going to be that big a deal.<P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||BBBAD GT||07-30-2000||11:22 PM||||I can vouch for the Vortech being a bulletproof piece.  I beat the living hell out of my A trim (bought it used), and still gave my 5.0 10lb of boost.  Now, my Strim is giving me 14-15lb of boost without a sweat.  <P>HYPTNOTiSE: What do you mean by a blow off valve?  Are you talking about the bypass valve?  The bypass is definately closed during any boost.  I've never seen a blow off valve (like the turbochargers use) on centrifugal blowers, but I'm mainly limited to 5.0's.  I'm sure glad you have a base program to start with on the DFI, and a friend to help.  Its not the most friendly system in the world (or the most advanced), but it does give you total control and I've seen some great results with it.  <P>Love that sig, espically with the N2O purge.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">  <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000014||HYPTNOTiSE||07-31-2000||07:55 AM||||yeah sorry i meant bypass valve. Accel is comming out with a new windows based gen 7 system in the next couple months. So i think it's going to catch back up to the rest of the market. Before this system soon to be released, things hadn't changed much since the 80's  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  My buddy's program is for a turbo, but i guess it's still a start.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> Yeah the sig is kick ass isn't it!<P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||1FST2M6||07-31-2000||08:22 AM||||no the rotrex units bypass valve is slow to react causeing a spike in pressure in the pulenum(sp) which their advertised HKS blowoff valve will remidy that spike. they says its an extra $200 included in the kit with the mounting bracket and piping mods already done... I've got a ProCharger if anyone wants one! ||||reg||1
